Actually, I think patience also helps.
Most of my recent deaths were due to carelessness such as "being caught in  
a summonning storm and trying to kill them all while standing on a magic  
portal" or similar stuff.

Now, I regularly reach Sokoban/Minetown and often go through to the deeper  
dungeon, dying by stupidity. (with warriors, I'm still pretty poor with  
magicians).
But since some time ago (probably since my 3rd ascencion or something like  
that (M, M[S], V, and recently K[S+Lethe])), I quite understand sentences  
such as "anybody can ascend a Valkyrie" (must be Derek's words, iirc).
Indeed, I feel like with a small amount of patience and care I would have  
no major trouble ascending a V, B, K, S or even M. I know how to handle  
the early game, I know that middle game is an exercice of care and not  
being too overconfident before reaching good enough HP and AC, I start to  
know where to fight and choose my position in open levels, I start to know  
the tricks that make the late game easy (eg levport to Sanctum+cursed GL  
to escape), ...
I'm certainly not a Marvin-class player, but I feel like if I had to, say,  
ascend 3 out of 10 V in a row I should be able to do so (no, I have no  
will whatsoever to try it for real...)

So, I guess there is a point in player advancement where patience/care is  
really a big advantage and has to be learned in order to progress further.

(and I still need to learn how to player magicians, even if I'm often  
playing them...)

Oh, and related to that, I also start feeling that certains conducts are   
indeed pretty easy to follow. My second ascencion was almost weaponless  
(magic lamp accident, but that's easier for M[S]) and almost vegetarian  
(eating after a killing spree and carelessness when choosing the corpse).  
My latest was wishless (even with 2 magic lamps before Mine's end) and  
polypileless. And indeed I really think that these 4 conducts (plus  
polyselfless) are pretty easy to follow while a couple years ago I would  
not have even try (and used magic lamp asap).

So, yes orcish barbarian is certainly an easier combination that most but  
patience and care are also important.

